Sharing, retry after a failure, caching of a success:
make: (computations: 0)
first force: pending (computations: 1)
concurrent force: pending (computations: 1)
first force: rejected with Failure("not configured") (computations: 1)
concurrent force: rejected with Failure("not configured") (computations: 1)
force after the failure: pending (computations: 2)
force after the failure: fulfilled with 42 (computations: 2)
force after the success: fulfilled with 42 (computations: 2)
An exception raised by the computation is retried too:
first force: rejected with Failure("not configured") (computations: 1)
second force: fulfilled with 1 (computations: 2)
Cancelling one caller does not cancel the others:
cancelled force: cancelled (computations: 1)
other force: pending (computations: 1)
other force: fulfilled with 7 (computations: 1)
A force from the failure handler of a caller runs it again:
force from the handler: pending (computations: 2)
force from the handler: fulfilled with 3 (computations: 2)
